= Overconfidence effect =

== Overview ==
The '''overconfidence effect''' is a family of calibration errors in which confidence exceeds accuracy or uncertainty is underestimated.

== Different phenomena ==
Overconfidence can refer to overestimation of one's performance, overplacement relative to others, or overprecision in confidence intervals. These are related but distinct phenomena.

== Measurement ==
A claim of overconfidence requires an explicit correspondence between confidence judgments and an accuracy or probability benchmark.

== References ==
* Baruch Fischhoff, Paul Slovic & Sarah Lichtenstein, calibration research.
* Moore & Healy, “The Trouble with Overconfidence”, ''Psychological Review'' 115 (2008): 502–517.

